+  //
+  // Our DOM components never navigate in place: real external links are handed to the OS instead
+  // (docxPreview/linkSafety, and the note editors' externalLinkClicked message).
+  //
+  // Scoped so it cannot be why a component fails to load: only main-frame navigations are examined
+  // (`targetFrame?.isMainFrame`), about: is allowed, and anything undeterminable fails OPEN.
+  //
+  // As on Android this is a scheme+host test, not a full origin check: port is not compared, and all
+  // file:// URLs have a nil host so one file:// path passes as "same origin" as another. That case is
+  // covered by the narrowed `allowingReadAccessTo` in load(request:) — WebKit enforces the grant as a
+  // recursive path-prefix match, so a file outside the bundle directory is unreadable regardless of
+  // what this hook allows. The two layers are meant to be read together.
+  //
+  // The comparison is against the CURRENTLY LOADED page, not against `source.uri`. Unlike Android,
+  // WKWebView routes programmatic loads through this hook too, so the initial load is examined here
+  // — and on iOS `source.uri` is RELATIVE in release builds ("www.bundle/<entry>.html", see
+  // expo/src/dom/base.ts, resolved against the main bundle by RCTConvert), so comparing schemes
+  // against it would reject the app's own first load and leave every DOM component blank. Anchoring
